  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1806.04 Road Skills Examination",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1806.04 Road Skills Examination.\n\n(a) The department shall determine whether the applicant has the ability to drive safely in a variety of on-the-road situations by administering a road skills examination.\n\n(b) The road skills examination shall consist of a qualitative evaluation of the applicant’s abilities and skills in performing all applicable maneuvers required for the vehicle being tested for and shall score no more than 30 points in the following general categories:\n\n(1) Left and right turns, including:\n\na. Approach;\n\nb. From stop;\n\nc. Turning; and\n\nd. Complete turn;\n\n(2) Driving in urban business area;\n\n(3) Lane changes;\n\n(4) Curves;\n\n(5) Roadside stop and start;\n\n(6) Intersections;\n\n(7) Railroad crossings;\n\n(8) Truck or bus signs;\n\n(9) Expressway or limited access roads;\n\n(10) Student discharge, if applicable; and\n\n(11) General driving.\n\nSource. #8405, eff 8-2-05; ss by #10523, eff 2-18-14, EXPIRED: 2-18-24\n\nNew. #13963, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-13-24; ss by #14100, eff 10-18-24, EXPIRES: 10-18-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1800.html"
